From 9f3fe4a8ea1ad726d7c14b41f7edf21958d25321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:59:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vpl-gpu-rt: Revert va_drm.h include path to this fork's
 nested libva layout

A real flashfiles build failed with a fatal file-not-found error:
libmfxsw.cpp includes "va/va_drm.h", which upstream intel-onevpl-26.2.3
changed from "va/drm/va_drm.h" (commit 1669afcc, enabling the upstream
release tag) -- assuming vanilla upstream libva's flat
<includedir>/va/va_drm.h install layout.

This fork's libva (hardware/intel/external/libva) keeps va_drm.h at its
original source-tree path, va/drm/va_drm.h, and exports it to
consumers via that exact include dir (Android.bp's libva_headers
export_include_dirs + this module's own -I flags). No -I flag in this
module's build resolves the "va/" prefix form against that layout.

Reverted both affected includes (libmfxsw.cpp,
libmfx_core_vaapi.cpp) back to "va/drm/va_drm.h" to match the actual
on-disk layout; this is the only form that resolves against existing
-I flags.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 _studio/mfx_lib/shared/src/libmfxsw.cpp  | 2 +-
 _studio/shared/src/libmfx_core_vaapi.cpp | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/_studio/mfx_lib/shared/src/libmfxsw.cpp b/_studio/mfx_lib/shared/src/libmfxsw.cpp
index eb2ea154..f410cf98 100644
--- a/_studio/mfx_lib/shared/src/libmfxsw.cpp
+++ b/_studio/mfx_lib/shared/src/libmfxsw.cpp
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <xf86drm.h>
-#include "va/va_drm.h"
+#include "va/drm/va_drm.h"
 #include <i915_drm.h>
 
 #include "mediasdk_version.h"
diff --git a/_studio/shared/src/libmfx_core_vaapi.cpp b/_studio/shared/src/libmfx_core_vaapi.cpp
index 6c3dadc8..5fc62c99 100644
--- a/_studio/shared/src/libmfx_core_vaapi.cpp
+++ b/_studio/shared/src/libmfx_core_vaapi.cpp
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
 
 #include "va/va.h"
 #include <va/va_backend.h>
-#include "va/va_drm.h"
+#include "va/drm/va_drm.h"
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 
-- 
